    "rationale": "K-outer ordering: each k-iteration first loads both A row-tiles into scratchpad rows 0-15/16-31 (persists across all n), then for each n loads B(k,n) to spad row 32 and computes both m-tiles. The m=0 compute stages B(k,n) via preload (accumulated=false), overwriting the accumulator at k=0 (out_addr bit30=0) or accumulating at k>0 (bit30=1); the m=1 compute reuses the latched B tile via a GARBAGE preload with accumulated=true. Every output tile therefore receives its three 16-deep partial products in strictly increasing K order (k=0 overwrite, k=1, k=2 accumulate), and the guarded mvout fires only on the last k. DMA traffic is minimal: each of the 6 A tiles and 9 B tiles is loaded exactly once (15 mvins, 3840 bytes), which is the lower bound since spad capacity (64 rows) cannot hold all A tiles across k. Command count is also minimal: 18 computes (one per output tile per k-tile), each requiring exactly one preload, plus 15 mvin, 6 mvout, 4 config, 1 fence = 62 commands."
